  <p style="margin-top: 50px;">Please see reverse side</p>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 14pt;">Requirements for Accounting Majors</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="section-title">Accounting Major Area Requirements: Students wishing to register for ACG 3101 and ACG 3341 must (1) pass both ACG 2021 and ACG 2071 with a grade of B or better, and (2) pass an Accounting Competency examination with a grade of 70% or better. For students in the FSU ACG 2021 class, the Accounting Competency material is embedded in the course as a final exam. Students transferring ACG 2021 (or its acceptable equivalent) from another university must register for the Accounting Competency Exam Canvas site. Please e-mail <span data-field="accounting_dept_email">{{ accounting_dept_email }}</span> to be added to the Accounting Competency Exam Canvas site.</div>

  <div class="section-title">Students must also earn a "C-" or better (i.e. not acceptable) in ACG 3101 as a prerequisite for ACG 3111 and all 4000-level ACG and TAX courses. Students must earn a "C-" or better in all other required upper-level accounting courses (prefix ACG and TAX). Any student not successful in obtaining the minimum passing grade within two attempts will not be permitted to enroll in that upper-level accounting course again.</div>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Course #</th>
        <th>Course Title</th>
        <th>Hrs</th>
        <th>Course Prerequisites</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for item in major_area_requirements %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ item.course_code }}</td>
        <td>{{ item.course_title }}</td>
        <td>{{ item.hours }}</td>
        <td>{{ item.prerequisites }}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="section-title">Additional Information:</div>
  <ol>
    <li>Students should plan to take all upper-level accounting courses in residence at FSU.</li>
    <li>In addition to the requirements outlined above, each student must complete all University-wide requirements for graduation. These requirements include liberal studies requirements, the multicultural requirement, the summer residency requirement, the FSU residency requirement, and total hours requirement. Depending on time of admission to Florida State University, University-wide requirements may differ; please consult your advisor.</li>
    <li>Students must not enroll in any course at another institution without first receiving approval from the College of Business Undergraduate Programs Office. Once enrolled at FSU, students should plan to take their upper-level accounting courses in residence at FSU. Students who are transferring upper-level business courses completed prior to enrolling at FSU must be from business colleges at other 4-year accredited institutions. These courses must be approved for course substitution by the College of Business Undergraduate Programs Office upon entering FSU.</li>
    <li>Requirements for CPA licensure vary by jurisdiction. The FSU Master of Accountancy (MAC) program satisfies the educational requirements for licensure for most jurisdictions. A 3.0 GPA in upper-division coursework as well as a 150 credit hour minimum are required. Students who are transferring upper-level business courses to the MAC program must have a 3.2 upper-division GPA, a 3.2 upper-division accounting GPA, and a 3.4 cumulative GPA to have the GMAT waived. Application deadlines for the MAC program are January 1st for fall admission; October 1st for spring admission; and March 1st for summer admission. Applicants interested in assistantships and fellowships should apply by March 1st. More information on the MAC program can be found at <span data-field="mac_program_url">{{ mac_program_url }}</span>. The MAC program division accounting GPA based on at least four upper-level accounting courses, and a 3.4 overall GPA are eligible for the BSA/MAC pathway. More information is available at <span data-field="bsmac_pathway_url">{{ bsmac_pathway_url }}</span>.</li>
    <li>Students who do not pursue the Master of Accounting program are encouraged to contact the National Association of State Boards of Accountancy (NASBA) or the board of accountancy for the jurisdiction they plan to become licensed in to determine the best path to meet educational requirements for licensure.</li>
    <li>For further information regarding the accounting major and scholarships for accounting students, contact the Department of Accounting, RBA 309, 850-644-2771.</li>
  </ol>
</div>
</body>
</html>